[Expected Approach] Using Deque - O(n) Time and O(k) SpaceThe idea is to maintain a rolling product of the last k terms using a deque to efficiently compute the n-th term of the sequence. The thought process is that every new term (from index k+1 onward) is simply the product of the previous k elements. We avoid recomputing the entire product each time by dividing out the oldest term and multiplying in the newest one.Steps to implement the above idea:Initialize k as the length of the input array and return the n-th value directly if n <= k.Use a deque to maintain the last k terms and a variable product to store their cumulative product.Fill the deque with the initial k terms, updating the product as you insert each value.Loop from index k to n, generating one new term per iteration using the current product.Append the product as the new term into the deque to extend the sequence.Remove the oldest term from the deque and update product by dividing it out.Multiply the newly added term to product and repeat until the n-th term is generated.
